            <ArticleTitle>Procedure-specific postoperative pain management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>107-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With 48 million surgical proceduces performed annually in the United States (Center for Disease Control and Prevention, 2012), posttoperative pain management is a significant health care concern for both patients and health care providers. Current information regarding assessment and treatment of postoperative pain is discussed, including recommendations from the Procedure-Specific Postoperative Pain Management (PROSPECT) working group.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
